Subject: [PATCH] MPEG: decoded pictures handed to the host, accurate colour, host costs

sceMpegGetPicture hands each picture it serves (RGBA, its index, PTS, VBlank tick, the game's buffer)
to a sink the game port may set (runtime/ps2_mpeg_native.h); when the sink draws it itself the
PS2-layout copy into the game's buffer is left out. sceMpegDelete tells the sink. An accurate
YUV -> RGB conversion (the chroma interpolated to every pixel across) can be chosen; the host
time of decoding, conversion and copies is counted. Nothing changes with no sink set.
(Transformers roadmap N6: native movies.)
diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_mpeg_native.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_mpeg_native.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dbc7c4b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ps2_mpeg_native.h
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+#pragma once
+// Movie pictures handed to the host (Kernel/Stubs/MPEG.cpp): the libmpeg HLE decodes each picture with FFmpeg; a game
+// port with a renderer of its own can take the picture as it is served to the game (sceMpegGetPicture) and draw it
+// itself, instead of reading the PS2-layout copy the HLE writes into the game's buffer.
+
+#include <cstdint>
+
+namespace ps2_stubs
+{
+    struct MpegNativePicture
+    {
+        uint32_t mpegAddr = 0;       // the sceMpeg object
+        uint32_t imageAddr = 0;      // the game's buffer the picture was asked into (sceMpegGetPicture's a1)
+        uint32_t width = 0;          // the picture's size
+        uint32_t height = 0;
+        uint32_t index = 0;          // its number in the stream since the decoder was made (0, 1, 2 ...)
+        int64_t pts90k = -1;         // its presentation time (90 kHz), -1 when the stream gives none
+        uint64_t vsyncTick = 0;      // the VBlank tick it was served at
+        const uint8_t *rgba = nullptr; // width x height RGBA, R first, alpha 255; nullptr: the decoder was deleted
+    };
+
+    // Called on the EE thread for every picture served (and with rgba nullptr when a decoder is deleted). Returns
+    // true when the host draws the picture itself and the game's buffer need not get the PS2-layout copy (the
+    // copy is written when it returns false, or when no sink is set - as before).
+    using MpegNativePictureSink = bool (*)(const MpegNativePicture &picture);
+    void setMpegNativePictureSink(MpegNativePictureSink sink);
+
+    // The YUV -> RGB conversion of the decoded pictures: false (default) = as before (swscale's fast path: one chroma
+    // value for each pair of pixels across), true = accurate (the chroma interpolated to every pixel across).
+    void setMpegAccurateColour(bool accurate);
+
+    // The host time spent on movie pictures since the last call (for the port's logs): decoding (FFmpeg's parser
+    // and decoder, the YUV -> RGB conversion included), the conversion alone, and the PS2-layout copies into the
+    // game's buffers; and the pictures served and copied.
+    struct MpegHostCosts
+    {
+        double decodeMs = 0.0, convertMs = 0.0, guestCopyMs = 0.0;
+        uint32_t picturesServed = 0, guestCopies = 0;
+    };
+    MpegHostCosts takeMpegHostCosts();
+}
